Lamlet idioms, verified: this file is also tests/fixtures/skill-examples.lam (a symlink), so `cargo test` checks
every `expect:` line below against the interpreter. Each expect line gives the next expression region's value.
Prose like this paragraph is ignored by Lamlet.

$[Import* std]

Functions, exact arity, explicit currying, first-class operators.
$[# {square x} {* x x}]
$[# {adder n} {^ {x} {+ x n}}]
${square 7} ${{adder 10} 5} ${map {' 1 2 3} {adder 1}} ${fold {' 1 2 3 4} 0 +}
expect: 49
expect: 15
expect: [2, 3, 4]
expect: 10

Local declarations (let*), and a zero-argument function called with {f}.
${{^ {x} [# y {* x 2}] [# z {+ y 1}] z} 5} ${{^ {} 42}}
expect: 11
expect: 42

Function definitions [# {f params} body] may recurse (a plain binding cannot); tail calls are constant space.
One declaration may hold several bindings.
$[# {fact n} {!if {= n 0} 1 {* n {fact {- n 1}}}}  ten 10]
$[# sumTo {^ loop {n acc} {!if {= n 0} acc {loop {- n 1} {+ acc n}}}}]
${fact ten} ${sumTo 100000 0}
expect: 3628800
expect: 5000050000

Records: literal, getter, setter, row-polymorphic access.
$[# p {. name "Ada" age 36}]
$[# {older r} {.age= r {+ {.age r} 1}}]
$[# {ageOf r} {.age r}]
${.name p} ${older p} ${ageOf p} ${ageOf {. age 3 other true}}
expect: "Ada"
expect: {age: 37, name: "Ada"}
expect: 36
expect: 3

Variants: #tag to build, match with a record of handlers (one per alternative), or !case with one clause each.
$[# {area s} {match s {. circle {^ {r} {* 3.0 {* r r}}} rect {^ {wh} {* {.w wh} {.h wh}}}}}]
$[# {perimeter s} {!case s {circle r {* 6.0 r}} {rect wh {* 2.0 {+ {.w wh} {.h wh}}}}}]
${area {#circle 1.0}} ${area {#rect {. w 2.0 h 3.0}}} ${#hello 1} ${perimeter {#rect {. w 2.0 h 3.0}}}
expect: 3.0
expect: 6.0
expect: #hello(1)
expect: 10.0

Options and pairs are ordinary std data.
${withDefault {some 3} 0} ${withDefault none 0} ${caseOption {some 2} {^ {} "none"} str} ${pair 1 "a"}
expect: 3
expect: 0
expect: "2"
expect: {first: 1, second: "a"}

Call sugar: x.f is {f x}; at a brace head the receiver is the first argument. Lexical, not type dispatch.
${"Hello!".substr 0 3} ${"Hello!".chars.length} ${{' 1 2 3}.map square} ${"a,b".split ","}
expect: "Hel"
expect: 6
expect: [1, 4, 9]
expect: ["a", "b"]

Control flow macros: lazy branches, short-circuit.
${!if {< 1 2} "yes" {error "never runs"}} ${!and true false} ${!or false true}
expect: "yes"
expect: false
expect: true

Templates: typed holes, expanded during the check into String concatenation, so a template is a String.
The text is exactly as written up to }": quotes need no escapes, and a hole may hold a String.
$[# who "Ada"]
$f"{Hello, $who! 2 + 2 = ${+ 2 2}.}" ${format "{} and {}" {' "a" {str 1}}} ${join ", " {' "x" "y"}}
expect: "Hello, Ada! 2 + 2 = 4."
expect: "a and 1"
expect: "x, y"
$[# {said p} f"{${.name p} said "${.words p}" ${str "(twice)"}}"]
${said {. name "Ada" words "hi"}} ${= f"{Hi $who}" "Hi Ada"}
expect: "Ada said \"hi\" (twice)"
expect: true

Formulas: a Latex is a record holding LaTeX source; `latex` makes one, usually from a template.
${latex f"{\frac{$who}{2}}"}
expect: {latex: "\\frac{Ada}{2}"}

Static evaluation and compile-time assertions.
$[# table [% {map {range 0 5} square}]]
$table ${!assert {length table} 5}
expect: [0, 1, 4, 9, 16]
expect: 5

Types are values; checking positions need static ones.
$[# Person [% {Struct {' {Field "name" String} {Field "age" Int}}}]]
$[# addInts {: {^ {a b} {+ a b}} {Fn {' Int Int} Int}}]
${.age {: p Person}} ${addInts 2 3} $[% {Option Int}]
expect: 36
expect: 5
expect: <none: Unit, some: Int>

Objects: records whose fields hold functions; instances from a prototype share the closure.
$[# {_greet self} f"{Hi, I am ${.name self}.}"]
$[# Animal {. name "nobody" greet _greet}]
$[# rex {.name= Animal "Rex"}]
${{.greet rex} rex}
expect: "Hi, I am Rex."

State transitions are pure functions; a fold over events replays them deterministically.
$[# {update state event} {match event {. inc {^ {n} {.count= state {+ {.count state} n}}} reset {^ {u} {.count= state 0}}}}]
${fold {' {#inc 2} {#inc 3} {#reset unit} {#inc 1}} {. count 0} update}
expect: {count: 1}

Animation as a function of time (sampled by a host).
$[# {ease t} {- 0.5 {* 0.5 {cos {* pi {clamp t 0.0 1.0}}}}}]
$[# {tween a b secs} {^ {t} {lerp a b {ease {/ t secs}}}}]
Floats are binary64: results are bit-identical on every platform, but not "nice"; format for display.
${map {' 0.0 1.0 2.0} {tween 0.0 10.0 2.0}} ${fixed {{tween 0.0 10.0 2.0} 1.0} 1}
expect: [0.0, 4.999999999999999, 10.0]
expect: "5.0"

Recursive types are declared with roll and unroll functions; a value is unrolled before it is matched.
$[Type {Tree a} rollTree unrollTree
  {Variant {' {Field "leaf" Unit} {Field "node" {Struct {' {Field "l" Tree} {Field "v" a} {Field "r" Tree}}}}}}]
$[# leaf [% {rollTree {#leaf unit}}]]
$[# {node l v r} {rollTree {#node {. l l v v r r}}}]
$[# {insert t x} {!case {unrollTree t}
                   {leaf u {node leaf x leaf}}
                   {node n {!if {< x {.v n}} {node {insert {.l n} x} {.v n} {.r n}} {node {.l n} {.v n} {insert {.r n} x}}}}}]
$[# {inorder t} {!case {unrollTree t} {leaf u {'}} {node n {flatten {' {inorder {.l n}} {' {.v n}} {inorder {.r n}}}}}}]
${inorder {fold {' 5 2 8 1} leaf insert}} ${Tree String}
expect: [1, 2, 5, 8]
expect: Tree(String)

User macros are hygienic syntax rewrites.
$[Macro !unless {{c a b} {!if c b a}}]
$[Macro !swap {{a b} {' b a}}]
${!unless false "ran" "skipped"} ${!swap 1 2}
expect: "ran"
expect: [2, 1]

Qualified names use `::`.
$[ImportAs std s]
${s::+ 1 {K::add 2 3}}
expect: 6
